       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day is about 214 mg/kg for a 70 kg patient. That is above the roughly 150 mg/kg single-ingestion threshold for acetaminophen toxicity, and it would be given every day. I know of no indication where this is safe, and the risk is acute liver failure and death. Once entered, the order could be given by nursing before anyone catches it.\n\nI can enter a dose within the safe range right now, such as 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 1000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum). If you meant a different dose or drug, give me the details and I'll enter that.\n\nIf you think this order is clinically justified, for example under a specific protocol, please check it with pharmacy first. Pharmacy can then enter it through a channel with the right safeguards."
